 =?UTF-8?q?=20one=20membership=20rule,=20and=20a=20machine=20edition?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A corridor names municipalities. Districts reach it through partOf, which is
the registry's own rule and was enforced from one side only — so five
districts sat in the corridor member lists as peers of the cities containing
them (GC-016). They are out of the fact list and back on every corridor
surface, under the municipality they belong to, derived by corridorStops().

The corridor pages and the proof map get machine editions and structured data
(GC-022): /corridors.md, eleven route twins, /where-we-work.md, and a
WebPage + Service + ItemList graph on every route page whose place nodes come
from the same hierarchy rule the area pages use.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
